Fix AWTK's CMake port: it never compiles src/lcd/lcd_sdl2.c, so the
AWTK_NANOVG_BACKEND=AGGE (software renderer) build fails at link time with
undefined references to lcd_sdl2_init / lcd_sdl2_texture_reset.

AWTK's own SCons build (src/SConscript) does compile that file, so this is a
plain gap in the CMake port. The file is only compiled by us for the SDL
software-rendering path, but adding it unconditionally is harmless for the
OpenGL build too (SDL2 is always a dependency of this build).

Applied by build_awtk.ps1 (idempotent); revert with:
  git -C third_party/awtk checkout -- cmake/src_libs.cmake

--- a/cmake/src_libs.cmake
+++ b/cmake/src_libs.cmake
@@ -53,6 +53,7 @@
 # --- base (src/SConscript) ---
 set(_base_src
   "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/src/lcd/lcd_mono.c"
+  "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/src/lcd/lcd_sdl2.c"
   "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/src/main_loop/main_loop_simple.c"
   "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/src/main_loop/main_loop_console.c"
   "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/src/lcd/lcd_nanovg.c"
